timeout_minutes":30},"commit_author":{"id":218610,"login":"trask"},"findings":[{"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### \ud83d\udfe1 Changes recommended\n\nThe claimed regression coverage for diagnostics and configuration-cache reuse is absent.\n\n<details open>\n<summary><strong>1 open finding</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Low severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Add tests for diagnostics and configuration-cache reuse](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20581#discussion_r4262565748) \u00b7 New\n</details>\n\n\ud83e\udde0 **Review effort:** Balanced","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5508260821","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5508260821},{"body":"[Testing] The stated regression coverage is not present in this change: the existing Gradle-plugin tests only exercise `AcceptableVersions` and `MuzzleDirective`, so neither the new diagnostic path nor configuration-cache reuse is verified. Please add a functional test with a lenient resolution failure that checks diagnostics appear only for a failing `assertPass`, the original Muzzle failure remains the task failure, and a second `--configuration-cache` run reuses the cache.","comment_commit_id":"2c9b1d89a7673cef295c91a4e022d9da364b7328","comment_id":4262565748,"key":"inline:4262565748","kind":"inline","line":396,"original_commit_id":"2c9b1d89a7673cef295c91a4e022d9da364b7328","original_line":396,"path":"gradle-plugins/src/main/kotlin/io.opentelemetry.instrumentation.muzzle-check.gradle.kts","review_commit_id":"2c9b1d89a7673cef295c91a4e022d9da364b7328","review_id":5508260821,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-13T18:37:14Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"thread_context":[{"author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"body_hash":"f273a7db5f3457d1ec1c76761ef40a27ef63e49ea6204b002955a6ea06d8a098","id":4262565748,"parent":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-13T18:37:14Z"}],"thread_id":"PRRT_kwDODJKVX86sAcsq"}],"frozen_at":1791939662,"frozen_at_iso":"2026-10-14T01:01:02Z","frozen_sha":"2c9b1d89a7673cef295c91a4e022d9da364b7328","head_ref":"copilot/trask-muzzle-resolution-diagnostics-b7b0ed","head_repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","head_repo_id":210933087,"input_mode":"direct","launch_run":{"actor_id":218610,"attempt":1,"id":38493374135},"loop_kind":"copilot_review","metadata":{"body":"<!--\nCHANGELOG.md is generated from merged pull requests. Do not add an entry unless this PR introduces\na deprecation or breaking change.\n-->\n\nFailed Muzzle `assertPass` checks currently hide exceptions collected during lenient dependency resolution. This change exposes those exceptions and their causes without changing compatibility decisions.\n\n- **Diagnostics:** Report resolution failures only when `assertPass` validation throws, then rethrow the original Muzzle exception. Successful checks and `assertFail` checks remain unchanged.\n- **Configuration cache:** Capture diagnostics as text rather than Gradle resolution objects. Regression coverage exercises the failure paths, successful lenient resolution, and cache reuse.\n\nResolution failures are diagnostic evidence, not proof of what caused a Muzzle mismatch.","title":"Expose resolution diagnostics when Muzzle assertPass fails"},"mode":"publish","pr":20581,"pr_author_id":198982749,"protocol":"git-candidate-v1","publication":{"auth_mode":"fine_grained_pat","authorized_actor_id":218610,"authorized_at":1791939664,"generation":1,"max_pipelines":5,"phase":"a8561ea604c643a6b660ead185dff79a","profile":"g